WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:14.489
Anne Frank was born in Frankfurt, Germany, in 1929.

2
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:20.280
She came from a well-to-do family and led a carefree early childhood.

3
00:00:20.281 --> 00:00:27.678
She played with her older sister, Margot, and dreamed of becoming a famous journalist or movie star.

4
00:00:27.679 --> 00:00:38.791
In her diary Anne eventually recorded an extraordinary story of perseverance and hope during one of the most horrific decades of history.

5
00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:45.373
Soon after Anne was born, Germany elected Adolf Hitler as its new chancellor.

6
00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:53.059
Hitler was a dictator who believed in a "pure" Germany and planned to eliminate all Jewish people.

7
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:59.422
This era is called the Holocaust, and it was a dark one for Germany and Europe.

8
00:00:59.423 --> 00:01:03.146
Life for Jewish people became increasingly hard.

9
00:01:03.147 --> 00:01:09.716
They were not allowed to work, ride on streetcars, or even live in some areas.

10
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:16.585
They were ordered to live in ghettos and made to wear large yellow stars to mark them as Jews.

11
00:01:16.586 --> 00:01:22.601
The ones who refused were sent to work camps, from which they seldom came out alive.

12
00:01:22.602 --> 00:01:31.712
Anne's family was not very religious, but they were Jewish, and her father, Otto, began to worry about his family's fate.

13
00:01:31.713 --> 00:01:38.769
In 1933 Otto decided to relocate his family to Amsterdam, in Holland.

14
00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:44.441
He became a director of the Opekta Company, which made fruit pectin.

15
00:01:44.442 --> 00:01:53.164
Things were different for Anne, but she resumed a fairly normal life, excelling at school and playing in her father's warehouse.

16
00:01:53.165 --> 00:01:57.350
However, this pleasant time did not last long.

17
00:01:57.351 --> 00:02:03.145
In 1939 Germany invaded Poland, starting World War II.

18
00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:11.287
Then, in 1940, Germany invaded Holland, and started sending Jews there to concentration camps.

19
00:02:11.288 --> 00:02:15.631
Otto Frank began to fear for his family all over again.

20
00:02:15.632 --> 00:02:23.394
He was forced to resign as Opekta's director, and Anne had to leave her school to attend an all-Jewish school.

21
00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:30.402
She and her sister were forbidden to visit museums, see movies, and even go out at night.

22
00:02:30.403 --> 00:02:36.558
Many of their friends were summoned to work camps in Germany, and none of them ever came back.

23
00:02:36.559 --> 00:02:40.040
The situation grew worse with each day.

24
00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:48.523
Since the family was not allowed to leave Holland, Otto began to think of a plan to hide his family until the war was over.

25
00:02:48.524 --> 00:02:54.245
He decided that the hidden rooms at the back of the Opekta warehouse would be perfect.

26
00:02:54.246 --> 00:03:02.356
The family called these rooms the "secret annex" since an annex is a smaller space attached to a bigger one.

27
00:03:02.357 --> 00:03:09.574
On July 5, 1942, Margot received a call-up notice summoning her to a work camp.

28
00:03:09.575 --> 00:03:13.323
The Franks knew the time to go into hiding had come.

29
00:03:13.324 --> 00:03:17.881
They left the next morning, trying not to attract any suspicion.

30
00:03:17.882 --> 00:03:23.659
Anne brought with her a brand-new diary she had received for her thirteenth birthday.

31
00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:29.883
She called her diary Kitty and wrote in it as if she were speaking to a friend.

32
00:03:29.884 --> 00:03:36.676
During the hard times that followed, Kitty became her best friend and closest confidant.

33
00:03:36.677 --> 00:03:43.068
The Franks hid together in the secret annex of the Opekta warehouse for two long years.

34
00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:48.636
They hid with another family and a Jewish man who was a dentist.

35
00:03:48.637 --> 00:03:55.060
At first no one knew how long they would have to hide, or if they would even come out alive.

36
00:03:55.061 --> 00:03:59.928
However, they had hope and a determination to survive.

37
00:03:59.929 --> 00:04:10.010
From time to time, Otto's former secretaries, Elli and Miep, sneaked through a bookcase, a secret door to the annex, to bring them provisions.

38
00:04:10.011 --> 00:04:18.846
Both Elli and Miep were extremely careful because if they were caught helping the Franks, they, too, would be sent to a work camp.

39
00:04:18.847 --> 00:04:22.317
Living in the secret annex was not easy.

40
00:04:22.318 --> 00:04:26.403
Anne and her family had to be very quiet during the day.

41
00:04:26.404 --> 00:04:31.061
They never went outside, and couldn't use a light at night.

42
00:04:31.062 --> 00:04:36.210
Sometimes Anne slipped up to the attic inside the secret annex.

43
00:04:36.211 --> 00:04:41.931
The attic's window gave her some fresh air and a quick glimpse of the blue sky.

44
00:04:41.932 --> 00:04:47.317
To pass the time, Anne wrote about daily life in the secret annex.

45
00:04:47.318 --> 00:04:56.095
She complained of the awful food they ate and described the tensions of living with so many people in such a cramped place.

46
00:04:56.096 --> 00:05:03.039
She even joked about it and called it "being on vacation in a very peculiar boardinghouse."

47
00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:08.196
Anne made her last diary entry on August 1, 1944.

48
00:05:08.197 --> 00:05:13.550
Three days later German police officers burst into the secret annex.

49
00:05:13.551 --> 00:05:16.812
No one knew who had betrayed the families.

50
00:05:16.813 --> 00:05:24.741
They were all arrested and sent to Auschwitz, a concentration camp in Poland where many Jews were killed.

51
00:05:24.742 --> 00:05:28.717
When they arrived, the men were separated from the women.

52
00:05:28.718 --> 00:05:32.564
This was the last time Anne saw her father.

53
00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:37.867
Anne, Margot, and their mother were forced to work outside in the brutal cold.

54
00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:42.837
They were hungry all the time and living in horrible conditions.

55
00:05:42.838 --> 00:05:52.194
In October 1944, soon after Margot and Anne were transferred to another camp near Bergen, Germany, their mother died.

56
00:05:52.195 --> 00:05:57.863
At Bergen, Margot and Anne again faced hard labor in the bitter cold.

57
00:05:57.864 --> 00:06:02.743
They were soon infected with typhus, a disease spread by lice.

58
00:06:02.744 --> 00:06:06.927
Margot died in February or March 1945.

59
00:06:06.928 --> 00:06:17.350
Believing that nobody from her family had survived, Anne Frank died in March 1945, barely two months before the end of the war.

60
00:06:17.351 --> 00:06:23.437
Of the eight people who hid in the secret annex, only Otto Frank survived the war.

61
00:06:23.438 --> 00:06:28.733
He traveled back to Amsterdam, where Miep had found Anne's diary.

62
00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:33.866
As Otto read his daughter's words, he felt her come alive again.

63
00:06:33.867 --> 00:06:38.677
Her candid portrayal gave a complete picture of their life in hiding.

64
00:06:38.678 --> 00:06:44.859
Otto wanted to share Anne's memory, so he published her diary as a memorial.

65
00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:51.830
Soon the little book became a symbol of survival for all the young people who lived through the war.

66
00:06:51.831 --> 00:06:57.009
Anne's diary was translated and published in many countries around the world.

67
00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:01.602
Today it is still a reminder of hope and survival.

68
00:07:01.603 --> 00:07:12.317
Although Anne Frank did not survive the war, her spirit keeps on living.
